A||||35||kel||bad news||||
Z||000000||kel||08-21-99||01:02 AM||||Well, after 25 years of a perfect record (no accidents) my good fortune ran out.  What makes it even worse is that it was my fault.  I was stopped behind 2 cars at a redlight in town and when the light turned green, everyone started moving.  (This particular light in town is known for malfunctioning and giving a green both ways.  I've almost gotten hit there before.)  Anyway, as I started to go through the intersection I always tend to look to my right(it's one-way) to make sure the cars are coming to a stop.  So I did and when I looked back the car in front of me had stopped and his backend was still partly in the intersection.  Apparently there was a car in front of him that had stopped for an "unknown" reason.  Needless to say, I hit him.  I was going maybe 10-15 mph.  My car was the only one with any noticeable damage, a dented nose.  Which brings me finally to my question.  The guy doing the work on it says he can't order the part from GM, so where can I tell him to look to get the nose for the 86 SE?  I miss my baby and want her back home in her little car house ASAP.  Any help would be appreciated.<IMG SRC="/ubb/frown.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>  
Z||000001||Patrick||08-21-99||02:10 AM||||<br>Hi Kel, <p>Sorry to hear that you had an accident, but the important thing is that you are Ok.<p>Cars are replaceable, people aren't. The fact that your Fiero has only suffered a dented nose is not that big of a deal at all.<p>A couple of weeks ago when I went to the wreckers to get an alternator, there were three Fieros in just that one yard. Multiply that by a dozen or more wreckers in EVERY town in North America, and I don't think there's any problem replacing the beak on your baby.<p>If the fella doing the body work on your Fiero is on the ball at all, he'll easily find a wrecker in your neck of the woods who has the parts you need.<p>Glad you're Ok. Let us all know how you make out with the repairs.<p><p><p> 
Z||000002||Cliff Pennock||08-21-99||02:47 AM||||Sorry to hear that Kel. I was in an accident myself about 6 months ago and the nose of my car had to be replaced too. I'm suprised to hear that guy saying that he can't order the nose from GM, because <b>he can</b>. I know, I was suprised as hell too that GM still had those in stock but they really do! My car has a brand new nose to prove it! It costed $400 (unpainted).<p>But it's probably cheaper to get a used one...
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||08-21-99||04:31 AM||||I just finished building my 88 not too long ago and about a week after it was done I was driving behind a slow van and switched lanes. I didn't see the guy speeding in the lane I pulled into, and when I looked in the rearview mirror, this guy was hard on his brakes. Inside the car were two guys with long hair and tattoos all over. Not very nice looking guys and I knew I was in trouble. At the next light I was expecting to see them pull me out of my car and beat the crap out of me in front of a dozen people. The passenger said a few words to me that I will leave to your imagination. After the light turned green, I turned off the main road. I was thinking about what almost happened to me a minute before and didn't see the car coming to my left, this car was speeding and ran a stop sign at about 45mph. I barley saw him and swerved just in time. If I had been hit by him I am pretty sure I would not be here spilling my guts like this, they would have had to pick them up off the street. Things like that put life into perspective.<p>I am glad you are OK and I'm sure your Fiero will be too. 
Z||000004||lowCG||08-21-99||11:53 AM||||Had a very similar incident myself a few years back,was driving a van with a large flywheel(1 1/2" thick,by 16" round)on the passenger's seat,traffic stopped,and when I slammed on the brakes,lightly tapping the car in front,the flywheel went straight for the front floor with a very loud "boom".<br>Thought I'd just smashed a car in a big way,turned out no damage was done.<br>If you're real lucky,you'll find a nose in your car's color!
Z||000005||kel||08-21-99||05:39 PM||||I appreciate your concern and telling me about your similar experiences.  Misery loves company you know!  It does put things into perspective though and makes you realize how quickly your life could change.  I'm thankful that it wasn't worse than it was.<p>Cliff,  I was wondering...did you order the nose for yours through your local GM dealership or some other way?  
Z||000006||Dave85||08-21-99||09:08 PM||||The Fiero Store has them for around $200-250.
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||08-22-99||03:06 AM||||I ordered the nose through the local GM dealer.
Z||000008||DXR_MOM||08-22-99||09:42 PM||||Kel, my heart goes out to you, I'm am so glad that you are okay.  It is wonderful that you have a team of Fiero pros to give you good advice.  You know that your car can and will be fixed.  Let me know when your baby is back to its' old self again.  Until then, be aware of your surroundings, drive carefully and stay safe.
Z||000009||ChadMan||08-23-99||07:31 AM||||Sorry about your mishap, Kel.  Ed Parks (email: fierofactory@juno.com) or Kick Hill Farm (email: rpark464@aol.com) might have your nose at a reasonable price.
Z||000010||Racer 1||08-23-99||11:34 PM||||Sorry to hear that Kel. I had a accident also about 3 years ago. I was going down the main strip when a police car coming from the other direction wanted to turn in front of some cars ahead of me. They stopped for the police car. The speed limit was posted 35 I was doing about 38. I was talking to my friend in the passanger seat then I looked up. Just in front of me were theses idiots stopped I slammed on my brakes just to find out my rear brakes were locked up but my front werent. It was kind cool like in slow motion hehe. The guy that I stuck had already been hit in the rear so his bumper was already pushed up. I got out to see the wreckage to my amazment no real damage to my front end except the paint spidered up on the front passangers side. Me and the guy I hit talked for about 2 minutes then we both took off. Gave me a good reason to repaint my front end myself. I also backed into a airborne express van once nothing major thow!
Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||08-24-99||12:30 AM||||Once I was getting a ride somewhere with a friend, it was icy, and he was going a bit too fast.. we hit a patch of ice and his car went off the road. Hit the ditch on one wheel and slid pretty far.. barely missed a tree. Took one tire off, and the rear bumper and exhaust.. course that happened when he tried to back the car up onto the road again, before he noticed one of the tires was off the wheel completely, and the hubcap was about to fly off.. No one was hurt and he got the car fixed. <p>Another time I was having a driving lesson in a blizzard.. the instructor kept telling me to go faster, even tho it was very slippery and I could barely see 5 feet in front of the car.. eventually I was going a bit over the speed limit (in town), and I really didn't feel comfortable going that fast under those conditions. He told me to take the next corner, so since I was about half a block away I started to slow down.. he said "no brakes.." I looked at him, and he told me to take my foot off the brakes... so I said ok, knowing what would happen.. I turned the corner, and before I could do anything, the stupid little Civic was stuck in a snowbank. No damage done.. took a while to dig out tho, the snowbank was at least 5 feet high, and the car was really stuck in it. heh.. soft snow, hit the snow on a 45 degree angle going about 35-40kph..<p>My friend who put his car in the ditch was also driving a Civic.... I don't like honda civics much.. for the usual reasons plus I've had some bad experiences with them.. :p
Z||000012||four50four||08-24-99||04:09 PM||||what did the instructor have to say?
Z||000013||Patrick||08-24-99||05:13 PM||||<br>DaRkLoRD, you do realize don't you that stories such as yours continue to perpetrate the myth that Canada suffers from ten months of winter and two months of poor sledding.<IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||08-24-99||05:55 PM||||LOL..<p>the instructor didn't say much, he just dug the car out and we kept going..<p>Patrick, you're right. We don't have 10 months of winter here. It's actually only 8. <p>hehe.. :p
Z||000015||SCCA FIERO||08-24-99||07:00 PM||||8 months of snow? I couldn't handle it. Here in Utah (where we have the world's greatest snow, it says so on all the license plates) we have about 5 months of snow and thats too long. 
Z||000016||four50four||08-24-99||07:31 PM||||you guys get summer? what part of canada do you live in? <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
Z||000017||DaRkLoRD||08-24-99||08:30 PM||||I'm from southwestern Ontario, right across the lake from Michigan.<p>4-5 months per year is about what we get here on average.. That's Winter. Now the rest of the year, depending on what part of Canada you're in, is either Bugs or Construction.... <IMG SRC="/ubb/wink.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
Z||000018||DJRice||08-25-99||06:56 AM||||Down here in Florida, We have 15 months of Summer, 3 of which Hurricanes are normally aimed at us......
Z||000019||kel||08-29-99||01:18 AM||||Thought I would give all of you who made suggestions an update.<br>The guy doing the work on it said he can't find a new front fascia.  He suggested that he re-mold the one I have now.  Said it would look almost new. It has no tears or holes, just a dent in the center.<br>I talked with Ed Parks from the Fiero Factory, and he said that 'hot tanking' restores the memory of the urethane and dents/sags will disappear.<br>I'm keeping my fingers crossed and will let you know how it turns out.<br>Thanks to all who tried to help!
Z||000020||Patrick||08-29-99||02:27 AM||||<br>"look <b>almost</b> new" ???<p>I don't know Kel, that sounds kind of scary. Will you have any recourse if you DON'T like the way it turns out?<p>If a new one can't be ordered any longer, I think you'd be better off to insist on a USED one in mint condition. Despite what you may have been told, they ARE available.<p>
Z||000021||kel||08-30-99||03:26 AM||||Patrick,<br>Paul (the guy doing the work on it) says if I don't like it, he'll keep trying to locate a new one and will do whatever I want.  He has done work on our cars before and did a great job, so I'm putting my trust in him.  Believe me, if it doesn't look good, I won't be happy.  And as my husband affectionately says..."if Mama ain't happy, ain't NOBODY happy!"<br>Ed Parks said it should come back "looking like new" after the hot tanking process.  Paul is suppose to start on it today, so I'll keep you posted.  <br>
Z||000022||Patrick||08-30-99||03:33 AM||||<br>Ok, we all have our fingers crossed. <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15><p>
