Z||000026||kel||09-15-1999||10:16 AM||||Hey Patrick,<BR>He still has my car.  I'm suppose to get it back this week.  He started painting it, finally, on Monday, so the verdict isn't in yet.  I did INSIST that he straighten the hood hinges, to set the hood forward where it was before.  He's been a real pisser about the whole thing, but when my husband speaks to him he's Mr. Nice Guy.  I'm tellin' ya, he doesn't like dealing with women too much.    I know I'm not too knowledgable about the mechanics of a car, but I do know what it looked like before the accident, I knew where every tiny scratch or imperfection was on that car. I take good care of it, and I just want it as close as possible to it's original state.  I run into the same thing at the shooting range sometimes, but the difference is, I can outshoot  most anyone that comes in there.  (I love to see that change in attitude after they see me shoot.)  Ah.... but cars... that's another matter.  That's why this forum is great.  Even though I don't have much to contribute, you are all very accepting.||||reg||1
Z||000027||theogre||09-15-1999||10:47 AM||||wish I could shoot here....... but when your favorite rifle sights in at 200 yards,,,,, it's hard to find ranges.||||reg||9
Z||000028||kel||09-15-1999||12:49 PM||||ogre,<BR>What do you shoot?  I've never picked up a rifle.  I only started shooting about 3 1/2 yrs, ago.  Joined a local indoor shooting range.  Took the handgun use and safety course.  Started out with a .22 semi-auto, graduated to a .38 cal, and after about 6 mos. I went to a 9mm (P 228)  After a year, I bought one. (I rented til I knew I could hit what I was aiming at)  I also love to shoot the .45 cal semi-auto. now.  (Sig Sauer P220).  Great gun!  That will be my next purchase.  Oh Lord, don't get me started on my handguns......too late!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">     ||||reg||1
Z||000029||batboy||09-15-1999||10:08 PM||||If "Mama" Kel can shoot and hit what she's aiming at with one of those big ol' awkward .45's, then I have a lot of respect for her (and I'm not messing with her either). I find them too heavy, too loud, and too much recoil. Different story about my Smith and Wesson 9mm though. I love it. Oops, wait a minute, I almost forgot this was a Fiero Forum. Hmmmmm. Ok folks, what's the best gun to carry in a Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000030||Cooter||09-15-1999||10:25 PM||||I am kind of partial toward my stainless Colt Combat Commander 38 Super for personal/car carry. You know- small car, small gun. My brother- the nice policeman- keeps trying to get me to carry a double action auto, but I just like the feel of the Colt. Oops, sorry Cliff, I just remembered- Fiero related only. . .||||reg||1
Z||000031||Patrick||09-16-1999||02:40 AM||||<BR>Geez, you Americans and your guns!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||4
Z||000032||Phil||09-16-1999||08:07 AM||||The wife and I have been in a pistol league for many years and both have NRA expert ratings although she's really close to making master (drat) so whats wrong with shooting?||||reg||1
Z||000033||ChadMan||09-16-1999||09:14 AM||||I love guns, and I love the Second Amendment.  (Somebody once said, "God made people...Sam Colt made them equal.")  But I'm really afraid that all these "shooting spree" maniacs (like the one in Texas yesterday) are going to make it harder and harder for lawful people to enjoy our firearms and protect ourselves in a safe and legal manner.<P>And I'm with you, Batboy.  You just can't beat a S&W 9mm.  Oh, and Fieros are great.||||reg||1
Z||000034||theogre||09-16-1999||12:21 PM||||I like to reach out and put a touch on things. My 22-250 is my favorite. less than 3 inch drop at 200 yards... talk about getting off the line. For a "slug gun" I like my 30-30. It's only good to about 100-150 yards tho. It's 150-170 grain bullets drop like stones.<P>I'm just about to start in with the hand guns. Nothing else you can shoot regular around here.||||reg||1
Z||000035||kel||09-16-1999||06:51 PM||||Brought my Fiero back this evening...finally.  It looks good as far as I can tell.  It was all wet from this rain, so when it dries off I'll get a better look.  The guy who did the work ended up apologizing to me after I confronted him with a few things.  And also I wanted to clear up something I had misstated before.  He did not have the money from the insurance company.  My husband had the check, but for some reason I was thinking he had paid him for parts already.  It feels so good to be in my car again.  Didn't realize how much I missed it!<BR>Now as far as guns go...<BR>I've shot S&W, Ruger, Beretta, Glock (the Mack Truck of guns), etc... but the Sig Sauers were made for my hand!  They're a little touchy, you have to get a feel for them, but once you do...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
